    "q-78765": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78765",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ find row operations that transform $A$ into the $3\\times 3$  identity matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's consider the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,{I}_{3}]$ where ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity. Then, by applying the following row operations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,{I}_{3}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  \\\\  & =[{I}_{3}\\,|\\,{A}^{-1}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operations are ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3},$ while\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
