    "q-78426": {
      "dom_id": "step-q78426",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
